A||||2||engine18||Jumping Engine||||11||
Z||000000||engine18||05-24-2000||04:01 AM||||I have used the forum search, with no success. I recently installed new poly ultimate dogbone into my 85 V6 Auto. But the engine continue to try and jump out of the car when shifting the auto transmission to drive or reverse. It's really bad.. There seems to be no problem with the shifting, just the engine reacting to the shift.  Thanks for any solution to the jumping engine.<p>[This message has been edited by engine18 (edited 05-24-2000).]||||reg||11
Z||000001||deceler8||05-24-2000||09:18 AM||||The dogbone bolt on the slotted engine side must be properly tightened or the engine will jump. The bone should remain stationary at all times.<P>The engine must also be "centered" prior to tightening the bolts...park on a level area and be sure not to push against the rear of the car while installing the bone/tightening the bolts.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Gold-86SE||05-24-2000||09:55 AM||||<BR>Also check the condition of your other motor mount and the two trans mounts.  If these are worn, excessive engine movement is possible.<BR>||||reg||1
